{"allow_collaboration":true,"allow_maintainer_to_push":true,"approvals_before_merge":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author":{"avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/12baa0a161b4dc39db50417c3669fc31659c207b91bdfaa0e73b610264f91faa?s=80&d=identicon","bot":false,"id":42084362,"locked":false,"name":"Srajan Gupta","public_email":null,"state":"active","username":"srajangupta1818","web_url":"https://gitlab.com/srajangupta1818"},"blocking_discussions_resolved":true,"changes_count":"3","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"created_at":"2026-09-12T19:05:41.840Z","description":"Closes #1364.\n\n`dsdv::RoutingProtocol::LookForQueuedPackets()` discarded the return value of `m_routingTable.LookupRoute()` and forwarded queued packets on the resulting default-constructed entry, whose route has a null output device. This crashed in `Ipv4L3Protocol::SendRealOut` (`NS_ASSERT(interface >= 0)` in default builds, a bare SIGSEGV in optimized builds).\n\nMirror the guarded idiom already used eleven lines earlier in `RouteOutput()`: when the lookup fails, log and `continue`, leaving the packets queued.\n\nAdds a regression test (`DsdvLookForQueuedPacketsTestCase`) on a three-node point-to-point chain that crashed deterministically before the fix and now completes. The test is a memory-safety regression: multi-interface DSDV still cannot route (the interior node advertises only `GetAddress(1, 0)`), which is tracked separately and noted in the release notes.\n\nVerified locally: the new test crashes (assert) with the fix removed and passes with it applied.","detailed_merge_status":"need_rebase","diff_refs":{"base_sha":"62a7c4c157ce59665a29e1013405af9c9a7f992c","head_sha":"71126010fb64c753670a3db49621cb0272028901","start_sha":"62a7c4c157ce59665a29e1013405af9c9a7f992c"},"discussion_locked":null,"downvotes":0,"draft":false,"first_contribution":false,"first_deployed_to_production_at":null,"force_remove_source_branch":true,"has_conflicts":true,"head_pipeline":{"archived":false,"before_